{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class GregAndFriends {\n    static int n, k, count50 = 0, count100 = 0;\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007;\n    static long[][] binom = new long[100][100];\n    static Deque<Integer> deque = new ArrayDeque<>();\n    static Map<Integer, Result> memo = new HashMap<>();\n\n    static class Result {\n        int steps;\n        long paths;\n\n        Result(int s, long p) {\n            steps = s;\n            paths = p;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        n = scanner.nextInt();\n        k = scanner.nextInt();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            int weight = scanner.nextInt();\n            if (weight == 50) count50++;\n            else count100++;\n        }\n        scanner.close();\n\n        computeBinomial();\n        int initial = pack(1, count50, count100);\n        deque.push(initial);\n        memo.put(initial, new Result(0, 1));\n\n        while (!deque.isEmpty()) {\n            expand(deque.pop());\n        }\n\n        Result finalResult = memo.get(0);\n        if (finalResult != null) {\n            System.out.println(finalResult.steps + \"\\n\" + finalResult.paths);\n        } else {\n            System.out.println(\"-1\\n0\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void expand(int state) {\n        int boat = state / 1000000;\n        int curr50 = (state % 1000000) / 100;\n        int curr100 = state % 100;\n\n        if (boat == 1) {\n            for (int take50 = curr50; take50 >= 0 && 50 * (curr50 - take50) <= k; take50--) {\n                for (int take100 = curr100; take100 >= 0 && 50 * (curr50 - take50) + 100 * (curr100 - take100) <= k; take100--) {\n                    if (take50 != curr50 || take100 != curr100) {\n                        long comb = (binom[curr50][take50] * binom[curr100][take100]) % MOD;\n                        int next = pack(0, take50, take100);\n                        update(next, state, comb);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        } else {\n            for (int take50 = curr50; take50 <= count50 && 50 * (take50 - curr50) <= k; take50++) {\n                for (int take100 = curr100; take100 <= count100 && 50 * (take50 - curr50) + 100 * (take100 - curr100) <= k; take100++) {\n                    if (take50 != curr50 || take100 != curr100) {\n                        long comb = (binom[count50 - curr50][take50 - curr50] * binom[count100 - curr100][take100 - curr100]) % MOD;\n                        int next = pack(1, take50, take100);\n                        update(next, state, comb);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void update(int next, int prev, long comb) {\n        int newDepth = memo.get(prev).steps + 1;\n        if (!memo.containsKey(next)) {\n            memo.put(next, new Result(newDepth, 0));\n            deque.push(next);\n        }\n        if (memo.get(next).steps == newDepth) {\n            long newPaths = (memo.get(next).paths + memo.get(prev).paths * comb % MOD) % MOD;\n            memo.get(next).paths = newPaths;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void computeBinomial() {\n        for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\n            binom[i][0] = 1;\n            for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++) {\n                binom[i][j] = (binom[i - 1][j - 1] + binom[i - 1][j]) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    static int pack(int boat, int a, int b) {\n        return 1000000 * boat + 100 * a + b;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <queue>\n#include <unordered_map>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint n, k, count50 = 0, count100 = 0;\nlong long binom[100][100];\n\nstruct Result {\n    int steps;\n    long long paths;\n    Result(int s, long long p) : steps(s), paths(p) {}\n};\n\nunordered_map<int, Result> memo;\nqueue<int> deque;\n\nint pack(int boat, int a, int b) {\n    return 1000000 * boat + 100 * a + b;\n}\n\nvoid computeBinomial() {\n    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {\n        binom[i][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++) {\n            binom[i][j] = (binom[i - 1][j - 1] + binom[i - 1][j]) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nvoid update(int next, int prev, long long comb) {\n    int newDepth = memo[prev].steps + 1;\n    if (memo.find(next) == memo.end()) {\n        memo[next] = Result(newDepth, 0);\n        deque.push(next);\n    }\n    if (memo[next].steps == newDepth) {\n        long long newPaths = (memo[next].paths + memo[prev].paths * comb % MOD) % MOD;\n        memo[next].paths = newPaths;\n    }\n}\n\nvoid expand(int state) {\n    int boat = state / 1000000;\n    int curr50 = (state % 1000000) / 100;\n    int curr100 = state % 100;\n\n    if (boat == 1) {\n        for (int take50 = curr50; take50 >= 0 && 50 * (curr50 - take50) <= k; take50--) {\n            for (int take100 = curr100; take100 >= 0 && 50 * (curr50 - take50) + 100 * (curr100 - take100) <= k; take100--) {\n                if (take50 != curr50 || take100 != curr100) {\n                    long long comb = (binom[curr50][take50] * binom[curr100][take100]) % MOD;\n                    int next = pack(0, take50, take100);\n                    update(next, state, comb);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    } else {\n        for (int take50 = curr50; take50 <= count50 && 50 * (take50 - curr50) <= k; take50++) {\n            for (int take100 = curr100; take100 <= count100 && 50 * (take50 - curr50) + 100 * (take100 - curr100) <= k; take100++) {\n                if (take50 != curr50 || take100 != curr100) {\n                    long long comb = (binom[count50 - curr50][take50 - curr50] * binom[count100 - curr100][take100 - curr100]) % MOD;\n                    int next = pack(1, take50, take100);\n                    update(next, state, comb);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        int weight;\n        cin >> weight;\n        if (weight == 50) count50++;\n        else count100++;\n    }\n\n    computeBinomial();\n    int initial = pack(1, count50, count100);\n    deque.push(initial);\n    memo[initial] = Result(0, 1);\n\n    while (!deque.empty()) {\n        expand(deque.front());\n        deque.pop();\n    }\n\n    if (memo.find(0) != memo.end()) {\n        cout << memo[0].steps << \"\\n\" << memo[0].paths << endl;\n    } else {\n        cout << \"-1\\n0\" << endl;\n    }\n\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00020287363440729678, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.00020323118951637298, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.372236667724792e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.13194595277309418, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.731181277544238e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.04388519376516342, -1.1